=============================
Bond lengths & Hirshfeld test
=============================

. The bond-detection criteria is the same as used
  by the Cambridge Structural Database (CSD).

. Hirshfeld test values are defined by:

     h_AB = n^T_AB (U^A - U^B) n_AB

  for bonded atom pairs A--B, where n = (r_A-r_B)/|r_A-r_B|
  is the unit vector from B to A. The units are Angstrom^2.

